---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Smart Fitness Mirror - Case Study" description="Fairest: Body Fat % Measuring Mirror & Caliper - Case Study.">
  <article class="max-w-5xl mx-auto py-16">
    {/* Header */}
    <header class="mb-16 border-b border-sage pb-12 text-center md:text-left">
      <div class="inline-block px-4 py-1.5 mb-6 text-xs font-mono font-medium tracking-wide text-sage-dark bg-sage-light border border-sage rounded-full">
        Interaction Design & Hardware
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6 leading-tight">Fairest: Smart Fitness Mirror</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-800 mb-8 font-medium leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        An interactive smart mirror and caliper ecosystem designed to accurately communicate body fat percentage and body shape transformations while motivating users to continue their physical activities.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 md:justify-start justify-center">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-800 font-medium">European Product Design Award</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-800 font-medium">FIT Award 2023</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-800 font-medium">Interaction Design</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    {/* Hero Showcase */}
    <div class="w-full bg-sage-light border border-sage rounded-xl mb-16 overflow-hidden">
      <img src="/src/assets/images/older-studio/Smart Mirror Project/Fairest 5.png" alt="Fairest Smart Fitness Mirror Showcase" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" />
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">1. The Problem Space</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-medium">
        Many individuals are health conscious and wish to see their health information (including fat percentage) displayed in a clear and digestible manner. Currently, there is only the use of smart scales, skinfold calipers, touch electronic sensors, and watch bands that can roughly calculate body fat. 
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-800 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-medium">
        Fairest exists to answer: <strong>What is the best way to visually and accurately communicate body fat percentage and body shape transformations?</strong> The overarching goal is habit-forming—to motivate and encourage users to sustain their physical activities.
      </p>
      
      <figure class="my-10">
        <img src="/src/assets/images/older-studio/Smart Mirror Project/Fairest 2.png" alt="Mirror Interface and UX" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200 shadow-sm" />
      </figure>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">2. Innovation & UX Strategy</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-medium">
        Unlike isolated diagnostic tools, Fairest tracks body fat percentage changes over time to instill positive habit-forming behaviors. By coupling the accuracy of a digital caliper with the ambient visual feedback of a mirror, the product transforms an intimidating metric into an approachable, encouraging journey.
      </p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-12 mt-8">
         <img src="/src/assets/images/older-studio/Smart Mirror Project/Fairest 1.png" alt="Fairest Detail" class="w-full aspect-square object-cover rounded-lg border border-slate-200" />
         <img src="/src/assets/images/older-studio/Smart Mirror Project/Fairest 6.png" alt="Fairest Detail" class="w-full aspect-square object-cover rounded-lg border border-slate-200" />
         <img src="/src/assets/images/older-studio/Smart Mirror Project/Fairest 8.png" alt="Fairest Detail" class="w-full aspect-square object-cover rounded-lg border border-slate-200 hidden md:block" />
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-6">3. Recognition & Awards</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-800 font-medium space-y-2 mb-8">
        <li><strong>Winner:</strong> FIT Sport Design Awards (Sport Equipment Design / Innovation)</li>
        <li><strong>Winner:</strong> European Product Design Award (EPDA)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 italic font-medium">Materials: Oak wood, high-contrast digital display, precision plastic molding.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
